worked_examples.solution:
(a) $\Delta H=50-80=-30$ units: negative, exothermic, because the products end up at a lower energy than the reactants. (b) $E_a=120-80=40$ units.

(c) The pathway must still rise from the reactant level to the peak before any product can form;

that 40-unit rise has to be supplied from somewhere (for example, colliding particles' kinetic energy) regardless of how much energy is released afterwards as the pathway falls to the products.

